1 ) what is the react ?
--- react is javascript library with composable UI components used to build to user Interfaces ---

2 ) what are react components ?
-- there are two types of components in the react 1. class component 2. functional component
class component -  A JS class that extend React.component and uses lifecycle methods and this.state
functional component - A simple JS function that return JSX and can use reract hooks


3 ) what is meant by React hooks ans what are they ?
-- Hooks are special functions that lets us use state and other react features in functional component ---

Examples for react hooks :- 
  useState -  used to manage the state of the component 
  useEffect - Runs code after rendering
  useRef - access or keeps a reference to a DOM element or value 
  useCallback - memorize a function so it doesnt get recreated on every rendering 


4 ) what is a prop ?
---- props are used to pass data from one component to another (this allows only one way data passing parent to child)

5 ) simple meaning of the JSX ?
--- javascript xml that lets us write html inside the javascript 


6 ) what is virtual DOM (VDOM) ?
-- Virtual DOM is lightweight copy of the real DOM . React upadates only changed parts in the code - making app faster.

7 ) what is react DOM ?
-- React DOM is a library that connect React with the web browser's DOM . It update and renders React components in the web page efficiently 


8 ) why react JS so popular ?
--  component based architecture 
